#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Optimize Slater determinant preparation for the latest version of Qiskit "
"Fermions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optimize Slater determinant preparation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"merge-slater-determinant-explanation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Optimize Slater determinant preparation {#optimize-slater-determinant-"
"preparation}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  The concepts in this guide are currently available only in the Python API. Equivalent functionality will be made available in the C API in a future release.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-initialize-"
"modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") gate declares a "
"reference mode occupation; an "
"[`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-orbital-"
"rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") gate rotates the "
"single-particle basis. Placed back to back, the two gates prepare a *Slater "
"determinant*; the modes start in the reference determinant and are then "
"rotated into the target orbitals. The "
"[`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-"
"determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gate captures "
"that composition, and because it carries the reference occupation, "
"transpiling it can use the rectangular "
"[`givens_decomposition_slater()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/linalg-givens-decomposition-"
"slater#qiskit_fermions.linalg.givens_decomposition_slater "
"\"qiskit_fermions.linalg.givens_decomposition_slater\"), which realizes only"
" the *occupied* orbitals, instead of the full square decomposition an "
"[`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-orbital-"
"rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") alone requires. That is"
" a strictly cheaper synthesis (see the payoff at the end of this guide).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The "
"[`MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-slater-determinant-"
"preparation#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation"
" \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation\") "
"transpiler pass detects the "
"[`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-initialize-"
"modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\")-then-[`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-orbital-"
"rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") pattern in a "
"[`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") and rewrites it into "
"[`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-"
"determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gates, so a "
"later synthesis stage picks up the reduced decomposition automatically. "
"Under simulation, the rewrite is a no-op on the state: "
"[`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-"
"determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") is *validate-"
"then-rotate* (it validates the reference occupation and then applies the "
"rotation, just as the two separate gates do), so the merge unlocks the "
"cheaper synthesis without changing the prepared state.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Throughout this guide, each circuit is drawn before and after the pass, side"
" by side: the input on the left, and the result of running the pass on it on"
" the right. Two helpers do that. `merge` runs the pass on a copy of the "
"circuit (through its "
"[`FermionicDAGCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-fermionic-dag-"
"circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicDAGCircuit "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicDAGCircuit\")) and converts the result "
"back to a drawable "
"[`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\"), and `draw_merge` draws both "
"halves into a single before/after figure:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What gets merged {#what-gets-merged}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The pass recognizes three patterns, all keyed off the block-spin mode "
"convention that [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-initialize-"
"modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") and "
"[`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-orbital-"
"rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") use. For a system with "
"`norb` spatial orbitals, the modes `0..norb` are the spin-alpha sector, and "
"`norb..2*norb` are the spin-beta sector. Slater determinant preparation is "
"done per spin sector because each sector has its own (electrons, orbitals) "
"shape.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Full-register (or spinless) {#full-register-or-spinless}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The simplest pattern is using "
"[`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-initialize-"
"modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\"), immediately followed "
"by an [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-orbital-"
"rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") on the *same* modes. "
"This is the spinless case (one determinant over all modes) and also a "
"spinful circuit whose rotation spans both sectors at once. The two gates "
"fuse into a single "
"[`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-"
"determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\"):\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A mode initialization and rotation fusing into one Slater determinant "
"preparation.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-"
"fermions/merge_slater_determinant-2.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Per spin sector {#per-spin-sector}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is the same shape, but restricted to one spin half. Here, two "
"independent initialize-then-rotate pairs, one per sector each fuse on their "
"own into a "
"[`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-"
"determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\"):\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Two per-sector initialize-and-rotate pairs, each fusing into its own "
"preparation.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-"
"fermions/merge_slater_determinant-3.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Global initialization, per-spin rotations {#global-initialization-per-spin-"
"rotations}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This entails a single full-register (`2 * norb`) "
"[`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-initialize-"
"modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") followed by *two* "
"[`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-orbital-"
"rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\")actions, one on each "
"contiguous spin half. The pass splits the global occupation at the sector "
"boundary and emits **two** "
"[`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-"
"determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gates. The two"
" rotations might appear in either order.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is the shape produced by the local unitary cluster Jastrow (LUCJ) "
"workflow (see the [LUCJ guide](lucj#lucj-transpilation)); A user places an "
"[`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-initialize-"
"modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") (typically the Hartree-"
"Fock reference by using "
"[`from_hartree_fock()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-initialize-"
"modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock\")) at "
"the front of the circuit and appends a "
"[`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-"
"ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\") ansatz, whose first two per-spin "
"orbital rotations directly follow the initialization once the ansatz is "
"decomposed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A global initialization with two per-spin rotations fusing into two "
"preparations.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-"
"fermions/merge_slater_determinant-4.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This pattern also fires when only *one* spin half is rotated by a gate "
"directly following the initialization, the shape produced when just one spin"
" sector’s orbital rotation happens to sit at the front of the circuit. The "
"rotated half becomes a "
"[`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-"
"determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") with its "
"rotation, and the other half is prepared with an *identity* rotation. The "
"identity preparation synthesizes to the reference X gates that the "
"[`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-initialize-"
"modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") would have emitted for "
"that half anyway, so padding it costs no extra gates while still unlocking "
"the reduced Slater synthesis on the rotated half:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A global initialization with a single per-spin rotation fusing into two "
"preparations.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-"
"fermions/merge_slater_determinant-5.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What is left untouched {#what-is-left-untouched}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The pass is deliberately conservative. It only fuses when the two gates "
"genuinely compose into a Slater determinant preparation, and copies "
"everything else through unchanged. “Immediately followed” is understood over"
" the circuit’s data-flow graph. The "
"[`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-orbital-"
"rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") fuses only when the "
"[`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-initialize-"
"modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") is its *sole* "
"predecessor across all of its modes. In the figures below, the before and "
"after are identical: nothing fused.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "An operation in between {#an-operation-in-between}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If any gate touches the modes between the initialization and the rotation, "
"they no longer compose into a bare preparation, so nothing is merged:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![An operation between the initialization and rotation blocks the "
"merge.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-"
"fermions/merge_slater_determinant-6.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A partial rotation that is not a spin half {#a-partial-rotation-that-is-not-"
"a-spin-half}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A rotation covering exactly one contiguous spin half of a full-register "
"initialization *does* fuse (see the previous section). But a rotation on any"
" *other* partial mode set (fewer modes than the initialization and not one "
"of its two spin halves, such as a sub-range straddling the sector boundary) "
"is not a per-sector preparation. Merging it would silently drop the "
"initialization’s role on the modes it leaves out, so the pass leaves both "
"gates in place:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A partial rotation that is not a spin half is left "
"unmerged.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-"
"fermions/merge_slater_determinant-7.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Why it matters: the synthesis payoff {#why-it-matters-the-synthesis-payoff}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The merge is worthwhile because "
"[`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-"
"determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") synthesizes to"
" far fewer gates than the "
"[`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-orbital-"
"rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") it absorbs. An "
"$m$-electron determinant over $n$ orbitals needs at most $m(n-m)$ two-qubit "
"rotations and no diagonal phase gates, versus the $n(n-1)/2$ rotations plus "
"$n$ phases of the full square orbital rotation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The preset Jordan-Wigner pass manager runs "
"[`MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-slater-determinant-"
"preparation#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation"
" \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation\") in"
" its optimization stage, so this reduction happens automatically. Transpile "
"a two-electron, six-orbital preparation all the way to a "
"[`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit)"
" and count its gates:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The preset runs [`MergeOrbitalRotations`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-orbital-rotations#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations\") immediately before [`MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-slater-determinant-preparation#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation\"). This matters when a *run* of consecutive [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") gates follows the initialization. The earlier pass first collapses the run into a single rotation, which [`MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-slater-determinant-preparation#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation\") then contracts with the initialization into one [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\"). Without that ordering, only the first rotation of the run would be absorbed and the rest would synthesize with the full square decomposition.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![The synthesized merged Slater determinant "
"preparation.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-"
"fermions/merge_slater_determinant-9.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compare that to synthesizing the same orbital rotation on its own. With no "
"preceding initialization there is nothing to merge, so the preset falls back"
" to the full square decomposition, which is deeper and carries diagonal "
"phase gates:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![The synthesized bare orbital rotation, with its extra phase "
"gates.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-"
"fermions/merge_slater_determinant-11.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The reduced decomposition drops all six phase gates and nearly halves the "
"two-qubit rotation count. The prepared determinant is correct up to a global"
" phase (physically irrelevant for state preparation), which is what the "
"phase gates would have fixed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Two ways to break the gate down {#two-ways-to-break-the-gate-down}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-"
"determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") can be broken "
"down in two different ways, and they are not interchangeable:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-"
"fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose\") "
"{#decomposehttpsdocsquantumibmcomapiqiskit-fermionscircuit-fermionic-"
"circuitqiskit-fermionscircuitfermioniccircuitdecompose-qiskit-"
"fermionscircuitfermioniccircuitdecompose}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Expands the gate into its *definition*: the "
"[`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-initialize-"
"modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") of the reference "
"followed by the full "
"[`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-orbital-"
"rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\"). This is equivalent to "
"the gate as an *operator*, for any input state.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`PrepareSlaterDeterminant.synthesis`, applied by "
"[`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/transpiler-"
"passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis "
"\"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") "
"{#prepareslaterdeterminantsynthesis-applied-"
"by-f2fsynthesishttpsdocsquantumibmcomapiqiskit-fermionstranspiler-"
"passes-f-2-f-synthesisqiskit-fermionstranspilerpassesf2fsynthesis-qiskit-"
"fermionstranspilerpassesf2fsynthesis}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Replaces the gate with the reduced decomposition of this guide. This is "
"equivalent to the gate only as a *state preparation*: it produces the same "
"determinant, up to a global phase, when the modes start in the vacuum. It is"
" cheaper precisely because it assumes that.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use the synthesis when the gate prepares a state on the vacuum, which is "
"what the gate is for and what the transpiler does for you. Use "
"[`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-"
"fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose\") when the gate has to"
" keep acting as an operator, for example because other gates precede it on "
"the same modes, or when you want to inspect or simulate the plain gates. The"
" [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/transpiler-"
"passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis "
"\"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") pass cannot know which "
"case it is looking at, so it is up to the circuit you give it to prepare the"
" determinant from the vacuum.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Simulating a circuit with ffsim needs neither: every gate applies its whole "
"unitary, so a circuit holding a "
"[`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-"
"determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") is simulated "
"as it is, and stays on the fast path for the "
"[`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"fermions/circuit-library-orbital-"
"rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation "
"\"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") gates around it. "
"Breaking only the Slater gate down with "
"`circuit.decompose(\"PrepareSlaterDeterminant\")` leaves those rotations "
"whole, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
